content.thinking:
Wait — there's an ordering issue in my fix. The HEAD/empty-body early return happens AFTER WriteHeader:

```go
	w.WriteHeader(status)

	// restore trailers...
	for field, vals := range trailers { ... }

	// HEAD responses...
	if r.Method == http.MethodHead || (buf.Len() == 0 && origContentLength != "") {
		return nil
	}
	_, err := buf.WriteTo(w)
```

That's fine — trailer restore is before the HEAD return, which is harmless (server won't emit trailers for HEAD since no chunking).

One more consideration: `dst[field] = vals` after WriteHeader — dst is w.Header(), the live handler map. finalTrailers reads it at handler exit. ✓

Also — `trailers[field]` lookup in the replay loop: `trailers` may be nil; `_, isTrailer := trailers[field]` on nil map is fine.

Now build and run the tests.

